-- English Comprehension: Grammar and Error Spotting
('SSC-CGL', 'English Comprehension', 'Grammar and Error Spotting', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Identify the error in the sentence: "She don''t like coffee."',
 '[{"text":"''She'' should be ''Her''","isCorrect":false},{"text":"''don''t'' should be ''doesn''t''","isCorrect":true},{"text":"''like'' should be ''likes'' and ''don''t'' should stay","isCorrect":false},{"text":"There is no error","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'With the third-person singular subject "She", the correct auxiliary verb is "doesn''t", not "don''t".'),
('SSC-CGL', 'English Comprehension', 'Grammar and Error Spotting', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'Choose the correct verb to complete: "Neither the manager nor the employees ___ available."',
 '[{"text":"is","isCorrect":false},{"text":"are","isCorrect":true},{"text":"was","isCorrect":false},{"text":"has been","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'With "neither...nor", the verb agrees with the subject nearer to it -- here "employees" (plural), so "are" is correct.'),
('SSC-CGL', 'English Comprehension', 'Grammar and Error Spotting', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Which of the following sentences is grammatically correct?',
 '[{"text":"He has been working here since five years.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"He has been working here for five years.","isCorrect":true},{"text":"He is working here since five years.","isCorrect":false},{"text":"He has working here for five years.","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, '"For" is used with a duration of time (five years), while "since" is used with a specific starting point in time (like a year or date).'),
('SSC-CGL', 'English Comprehension', 'Grammar and Error Spotting', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Choose the correct form to complete: "If I ___ rich, I would travel the world."',
 '[{"text":"am","isCorrect":false},{"text":"was","isCorrect":false},{"text":"were","isCorrect":true},{"text":"be","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'In a hypothetical (subjunctive mood) conditional sentence, "were" is used regardless of subject, as in "If I were rich...".'),

